    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Что он сказал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What did he say?' The first content word means 'what', and 'said' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Он сказал нам уходить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He told us to leave.' Notice the word order: 'he' comes first, and 'to leave' finishes the sentence. And Chef jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Я не верю в это.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not believe this.' Here 'I' sets up the idea, while 'this' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это конец?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Is this the end?' You'll hear 'this' all the time in the show, here connected with 'end'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Я не знаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not know.' The key word here means 'I', which Chef combines with 'know'. Maks answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Шеф, что делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, what to do?' Maks starts with 'chef' and pairs it with 'what' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Мы должны уйти.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We must leave.' In Russian, 'we' leads into 'to leave' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мне очень жаль.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am very sorry.' Anya starts with 'to me' and pairs it with 'very much' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Собирайтесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Pack your things.' The first content word means 'to intend', and 'to intend' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извините.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am sorry.' The key word here means 'sorry', which Anya combines with 'sorry'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это мой долг.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is my duty.' Listen for the word meaning 'this' right alongside 'debt' in this line. And Chef jumps in.",
